canadian lex brakovsky is embarking on a  dangerous journey packing this van full  of supplies from baby food to body armor  and driving it to the front lines in  ukraine watching it from from my home in  canada was just driving me nuts like it  was hard to  to watch it and not do anything about it  six weeks ago brakovsky was here on his  boat in nova scotia the lobster  fisherman moved to canada 30 years ago  but grew up in ukraine within days of  russia's invasion he flew to poland and  met a local aid group looking for  drivers willing to travel to the front  lines they need people that are willing  to go more than they need money i think  because there isn't too many people that  that are  you know ready to to drive to places  like that and for good reason last month  berkowski delivered aid to this city  near the russian border he then filled  his van with women and children and was  driving them out when his vehicle came  under attack all we've seen is just  explosions right right right in front of  us he and hundreds of others were  trapped he spoke to global news from  their shelter we tried to get out three  times yesterday but every time we get we  get anywheres or  right away under constant shelling  there's absolutely no power no heat  no  very limited water supply finally after  five days of failed attempts he managed  to escape  back to the relative safety of levive in  western ukraine after a few hours of  sleep he headed back to the front lines  with another shipment of aid we need  this help an adviser to the ukrainian  president had this message for other  ukrainian canadians for the many leaders  of the ukrainian  diaspora in canada  maybe it's time to come to ukraine  global news met many canadians answering  that call from the ukrainian government  from all walks of life i was actually  in a way pleasantly surprised  that so many canadians have have come  here this canadian ukrainian  entrepreneur is now handling logistics  and procurement for ukraine's volunteer  defense forces this millwright from bc  isn't even ukrainian but he's taking six  weeks unpaid leave to deliver aid and  rescue civilians these people have been  fighting the further democracy and i  just couldn't stand for the russians to  come back and take that all away from  them ottawa is advising canadians to  avoid all travel to ukraine but these  volunteers say staying home wasn't an  option  jeff semple global news toronto
 

